      "made": {
        "kind": "reply",
        "text": "**7 days from delivery works well for most handloom saree stores.** It gives buyers time to check colour, weave and drape in person, and keeps unsold stock from sitting in transit for weeks. Many Indian textile sellers use 7 days. Some go up to 10–15 days for premium silks to build trust.\n\nConditions that protect you on handloom pieces:\n\n- **Unworn and unwashed**, with tags and the original fold or packaging intact.\n- **No returns on altered pieces**, such as a stitched fall or pico, a blouse cut from the attached piece, or custom dyeing.\n- **Exchange or store credit only** for sale items, if you'd like to protect margins.\n- **Say plainly that handloom variation isn't a defect.** Slight irregularities in weave, colour or motif are what make it handmade.\n- **Ask for an unboxing video for damage claims.** This is common in India and settles disputes quickly.\n\nIf your sarees are mostly high-value silks such as Kanjeevaram or Banarasi, 10 days with a quality check on return is a fair middle ground. I can also turn this into a return policy for your store.",
